      "rationale": "Placed close to the module VCC pin; the pair with C1 is standard practice. Alternatives: any 25 V X7R part.",
      "datasheet": "kemet-c-series",
      "symbol": "capacitor"
    },
    {
      "ref": "R2",
      "value": "4.7 kΩ 1 %",
      "part": "Yageo RC0603FR-074K7L",
      "manufacturer": "Yageo",
      "function": "I2C pull-up, SDA, to 3.3 V",
      "ratings": {
        "resistance_ohm": 4700,
        "power_w": 0.1
      },
      "pins": [
        {
          "number": "1",
          "name": "to 3V3",
          "net": "3V3"
        },
        {
          "number": "2",
          "name": "to SDA",
          "net": "SDA"
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "4.7 kΩ is the usual pull-up for 100 kHz I2C at 3.3 V; it keeps the rise time inside the specification while not loading the bus. Pulling up to 3.3 V — the same rail as the ESP32 and the sensor — is what keeps the bus voltage-safe. Alternatives: 2.2 kΩ for faster edges or longer wiring (more current), 10 kΩ for very low power (slower edges).",
      "datasheet": "yageo-rc",
      "symbol": "resistor"
    },
    {
